# Agent coordination (parallel work)

Use when spawning **multiple agents** from one user request.

## Workflow

1. Create `cursor/sprint-<N>-<topic>-integration-13e3` from `main`.
2. Publish **file ownership map** in `docs/debt/refactoring-log.md` before spawning agents.
3. **Foundation agent first** (if needed): shared `api.ts`, fixtures, CI scripts — merge to integration.
4. Spawn parallel agents on **disjoint paths** only.
5. Each agent: branch from integration → work → push → verify tip on correct branch.
6. Operator merges agent branches into integration (or cherry-pick on mix-up).
7. Single PR: integration → `main` when sprint exit criteria met.

## File ownership (default splits)

| Agent | Owns | Avoid |
|-------|------|-------|
| E2E health | `e2e/**/health*`, `health.tracking.spec.ts` | `api.ts` after foundation merge |
| E2E auth/pet | `auth.*.spec.ts`, `pet.profiles.spec.ts`, related pages | vet, org specs |
| E2E org | `organisation*.spec.ts`, adoption specs | sharing, api.ts |
| Node routes | `server/routes/<domain>/` | other domains |
| Flutter screen | `lib/features/<domain>/presentation/screens/<one>/` | same feature widgets unless assigned |
| Governance | `scripts/`, `.github/`, `docs/quality/` | product code |

## Post-agent checklist

```bash
git fetch origin
git log --oneline origin/<expected-branch> -5
# Confirm commit messages match the agent's task
```

If commits appear on the wrong branch, **cherry-pick** onto integration; do not re-run full work.

## Anti-patterns

- Two agents editing `e2e/playwright/support/api.ts` concurrently
- Multiple agents committing to the same branch name without pull/rebase
- Merging agents directly to `main` (bypasses integration batching)
- Spawning agents before ownership map is written
